        <activityName xml:lang="en">Tower server, at data center</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Tower server, at data center
The tower server contains various electronic components and hardware; UUID: 2de839ed-bb09-3ac8-942c-264aa5a5075c
The dataset is based on one tower server (i.e., HP ProLiant ML350p Gen8). Generally, public information on tower servers are quite limited when compared to other server types (rack, blade). Nevertheless, the model is built on the inventory modeling concepts and assumptions borrowed from other server types.
Location: Typical tower servers.
Technology: Tower servers used in the data centers.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: Average technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2de839ed-bb09-3ac8-942c-264aa5a5075c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
